  "summary": "Six database updates pair expanded structure, ligand and disorder annotation with versioned APIs, MCP servers and workflows for programmatic and agentic access.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is structure-linked annotation resources growing in content while becoming easier to query computationally. CATH and TED broaden superfamily number and diversity by integrating PDB and AlphaFold structures. GPCRdb adds structure and ligand data, including Boltz-2 and AlphaFold2-Multimer models. PDBe extends literature-mined residue annotations, links MD simulation data via MDposit, adds MOLE pore analyses, and offers API and MCP agentic access. MobiDB adds a versioned REST API, an MCP server, Nextflow workflows and static datasets. HIPPIE 3.0 expands experimentally supported human PPIs to about 1.2M and adds negative training sets. The Chemical Probes Portal, with 26% more curated probes, is expert-reviewed and fits this thread more loosely.",
